00:50:05,500 --> 00:50:06,957
There's the weight of
a hundred-year-old business

771
00:50:06,958 --> 00:50:08,875
on my father's shoulders.

772
00:50:10,166 --> 00:50:11,874
And on mine.

773
00:50:17,500 --> 00:50:18,833
<i>Watch your step.</i>

774
00:50:23,833 --> 00:50:25,999
This is where you live?

775
00:50:26,000 --> 00:50:29,374
Yep. I've been living
on this boat for so long,

776
00:50:29,375 --> 00:50:33,415
it's hard to fall asleep
without the sea underneath me.

777
00:50:33,416 --> 00:50:34,832
Mm.

778
00:50:34,833 --> 00:50:36,833
Was your mom ever around?

779
00:50:38,833 --> 00:50:41,458
She... she died when I was eight.

780
00:50:43,458 --> 00:50:44,875
I'm sorry.

781
00:50:46,625 --> 00:50:49,791
Oh, here's the old man.

782
00:50:51,500 --> 00:50:52,583
Come here.

783
00:50:53,750 --> 00:50:56,041
You have to meet Oriah.

784
00:50:56,833 --> 00:50:58,208
Hello, Oriah.

785
00:50:58,750 --> 00:51:00,832
-My son has told me a lot about you.
-In English, Dad.

786
00:51:00,833 --> 00:51:01,957
I'm sorry.

787
00:51:01,958 --> 00:51:04,165
-I'm Mateo.
-Ry.

788
00:51:04,166 --> 00:51:06,125
Nice to meet you.

789
00:51:08,583 --> 00:51:10,333
Um, have we met before? You look familiar.

790
00:51:12,000 --> 00:51:14,457
No, I don't think so.
It's my first time here.

791
00:51:14,458 --> 00:51:15,707
Don't be weird.

792
00:51:15,708 --> 00:51:17,624
We were about to go for a ride.

793
00:51:17,625 --> 00:51:19,499
Okay. Have fun.

794
00:51:19,500 --> 00:51:21,833
Thank you.

795
00:51:22,875 --> 00:51:25,124
Ready to work?

796
00:51:25,125 --> 00:51:28,082
-Work?
-Mm-hmm.

797
00:51:28,083 --> 00:51:30,874
-Yes, sir.
-Let's go.

798
00:51:34,000 --> 00:51:35,750
Listen up.

799
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:37,540
This is Oriah.

800
00:51:37,541 --> 00:51:39,499
She'll be helping out today, all right?

801
00:51:39,500 --> 00:51:42,000
You've never brought a girl
on board before.

802
00:51:44,541 --> 00:51:46,624
-What'd he say?
-Nothing. Okay!

803
00:51:46,625 --> 00:51:47,865
Let's get to work.

804
00:51:50,083 --> 00:51:51,540
Not the small ones, okay?

805
00:51:51,541 --> 00:51:52,874
Okay, got it.

806
00:51:52,875 --> 00:51:55,833
Why should they die if we can't eat them?

807
00:51:59,500 --> 00:52:01,749
You're a natural.

808
00:52:01,750 --> 00:52:03,749
Hmm.

809
00:52:07,625 --> 00:52:09,082
Good job.

810
00:52:11,541 --> 00:52:14,750
I don't think I've ever smelled this bad
in my whole life.

811
00:52:17,375 --> 00:52:18,583
Let's clean up, then.

812
00:52:27,375 --> 00:52:28,499
Come in.

813
00:52:28,500 --> 00:52:30,540
The water is amazing.

814
00:52:30,541 --> 00:52:32,040
Are there sharks in there?

815
00:52:32,041 --> 00:52:33,999
Of course. It's the sea.

816
00:52:34,000 --> 00:52:35,665
Come on!

817
00:52:35,666 --> 00:52:38,290
I thought you didn't scare easily.

818
00:53:04,291 --> 00:53:06,374
Ah.

819
00:53:07,625 --> 00:53:09,874
<i>Gràcies, Julian.</i>

820
00:53:09,875 --> 00:53:12,665
You make your father proud.

821
00:53:12,666 --> 00:53:13,666
<i>Gràcies.</i>

822
00:53:21,208 --> 00:53:24,625
And now we get to enjoy
the fruits of our labor.

823
00:53:25,708 --> 00:53:28,583
This is the best fish you'll ever try.

824
00:53:37,041 --> 00:53:38,499
Mmm.

825
00:53:38,500 --> 00:53:39,915
-Oh, my God, it is really good.
-See?

826
00:53:39,916 --> 00:53:42,582
Mm-hmm. It's, like, sweet and buttery.

827
00:53:42,583 --> 00:53:44,999
And good for you, too.

828
00:53:47,916 --> 00:53:49,791
Mmm.

829
00:53:52,375 --> 00:53:54,541
You really love what you do, don't you?

830
00:53:57,250 --> 00:54:00,040
What's not to love?

831
00:54:00,041 --> 00:54:03,124
I get to live on the sea,

832
00:54:03,125 --> 00:54:05,207
work alongside my family,

833
00:54:05,208 --> 00:54:07,040
swim, fish.

834
00:54:07,041 --> 00:54:10,249
I get to honor my dad,

835
00:54:10,250 --> 00:54:12,415
my grandpa.

836
00:54:12,416 --> 00:54:14,125
I've never even met my dad.

837
00:54:15,791 --> 00:54:17,790
-Really?
-Yeah.

838
00:54:17,791 --> 00:54:20,165
He's a businessman from Texas
that couldn't be bothered.

839
00:54:20,166 --> 00:54:23,290
But my mom is awesome.

840
00:54:23,291 --> 00:54:27,625
She left Mallorca to pursue the...
the American dream.

841
00:54:28,666 --> 00:54:30,874
When she arrived to the States,
she had nothing.

842
00:54:30,875 --> 00:54:34,041
But she worked her ass off, and...

843
00:54:37,291 --> 00:54:39,125
what she's accomplished
is pretty amazing.

844
00:54:40,916 --> 00:54:42,375
She's had a lot of success and...

845
00:54:43,416 --> 00:54:45,207
What?

846
00:54:45,208 --> 00:54:47,540
I'm so sorry, but...

847
00:54:47,541 --> 00:54:48,957
it just surprise me sometimes

848
00:54:48,958 --> 00:54:51,999
what Americans define as success.

849
00:54:52,000 --> 00:54:53,666
What do you mean?

850
00:54:55,000 --> 00:54:58,999
I mean, it seems like
you just work and work

851
00:54:59,000 --> 00:55:01,040
just to go on vacation

852
00:55:01,041 --> 00:55:03,583
and then buy more and more and...

853
00:55:05,000 --> 00:55:06,915
I don't know. Look at our lives here.

854
00:55:06,916 --> 00:55:07,957
Mm-hmm.

855
00:55:07,958 --> 00:55:09,124
Sure, we have problems,

856
00:55:09,125 --> 00:55:12,999
but we are more than happy
with what we have.

857
00:55:13,000 --> 00:55:14,332
What else could we want?

858
00:55:14,333 --> 00:55:17,041
Even Miss America ended up on my boat.

859
00:55:18,500 --> 00:55:23,207
Sometimes you just
have to enjoy what you have

860
00:55:23,208 --> 00:55:24,958
while you have it.

861
00:55:26,750 --> 00:55:28,291
Does that make sense?

862
00:55:31,416 --> 00:55:33,250
More than you know.

863
00:55:35,708 --> 00:55:37,750
Being here...

864
00:55:39,708 --> 00:55:42,874
this place, this summer, it's...

865
00:55:42,875 --> 00:55:45,375
really made me think about
where I want to be.

866
00:55:49,083 --> 00:55:51,082
Well...

867
00:55:51,083 --> 00:55:55,666
there's never been anywhere else on Earth
I want to be than right here.

868
00:56:08,166 --> 00:56:10,000
Can I see your room?

869
00:56:25,541 --> 00:56:27,916
<i>♪ You could never die ♪</i>

870
00:56:29,041 --> 00:56:32,041
<i>♪ I'll always keep you alive ♪</i>

871
00:56:33,666 --> 00:56:36,375
<i>♪ Think about you all the time ♪</i>

872
00:56:37,875 --> 00:56:40,708
<i>♪ My security in life ♪</i>

873
00:56:42,416 --> 00:56:44,916
<i>♪ And when I'm low ♪</i>

874
00:56:46,291 --> 00:56:49,416
<i>♪ you get me high like coke ♪</i>

875
00:56:50,958 --> 00:56:53,375
<i>♪ How could I let you go? ♪</i>

876
00:56:55,291 --> 00:56:56,708
<i>♪ I'll never know ♪</i>

877
00:56:57,750 --> 00:57:02,499
<i>♪ You could play me like a song ♪</i>

878
00:57:02,500 --> 00:57:06,457
<i>♪ and I'll still sing along ♪</i>

879
00:57:06,458 --> 00:57:10,082
<i>♪ The only tune I know...</i>

880
00:57:11,541 --> 00:57:14,916
<i>♪ Love you till we're bones ♪</i>

881
00:57:16,708 --> 00:57:20,957
<i>♪ What else can I say? ♪</i>

882
00:57:20,958 --> 00:57:25,249
<i>♪ Another time maybe ♪</i>

883
00:57:25,250 --> 00:57:28,332
<i>♪ And I don't got the heart ♪</i>

884
00:57:28,333 --> 00:57:32,041
<i>♪ to leave you in this way ♪</i>

885
00:57:33,791 --> 00:57:38,165
<i>♪ Another heartbreak ♪</i>

886
00:57:38,166 --> 00:57:42,415
<i>♪ The cycle breaks me ♪</i>

887
00:57:42,416 --> 00:57:45,457
<i>♪ I have myself to blame ♪</i>

888
00:57:45,458 --> 00:57:49,457
<i>♪ for hurting in this way ♪</i>

889
00:57:49,458 --> 00:57:53,957
<i>♪ You could play me like a song ♪</i>

890
00:57:53,958 --> 00:57:58,415
<i>♪ and I'll still sing along ♪</i>

891
00:57:58,416 --> 00:58:01,833
<i>♪ Hold you till we're bones ♪</i>

892
00:58:02,833 --> 00:58:06,625
<i>♪ Hold you till we're bones ♪</i>

893
00:58:11,083 --> 00:58:14,916
<i>♪ Hold you till we're bones ♪</i>

894
00:58:19,875 --> 00:58:22,374
<i>♪ Hold you till we're bones ♪</i>

895
00:58:27,583 --> 00:58:29,582
Okay, um, do you mind having...

896
00:58:29,583 --> 00:58:31,499
Oh. Hi.

897
00:58:31,500 --> 00:58:33,290
-How are you feeling?
-Great.

898
00:58:33,291 --> 00:58:35,290
You look radiant and happy.

899
00:58:35,291 --> 00:58:37,541
I am.

900
00:58:40,375 --> 00:58:41,957
Okay, I don't want to know.

901
00:58:41,958 --> 00:58:43,374
As long as you're being safe.

902
00:58:43,375 --> 00:58:44,790
You don't know
these Spanish boys like I do.

903
00:58:44,791 --> 00:58:45,999
Had I stayed on this island,

904
00:58:46,000 --> 00:58:48,165
Lord knows how many brothers
and sisters you'd have.

905
00:58:48,166 --> 00:58:50,332
Mom, please.

906
00:58:50,333 --> 00:58:51,665
Uh, if you have a second,

907
00:58:51,666 --> 00:58:53,915
I would love to talk to you
about the dance company.

908
00:58:53,916 --> 00:58:55,874
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Sorry.

909
00:58:55,875 --> 00:58:57,582
Oh, no,
I don't like it. That one.

910
00:58:57,583 --> 00:58:59,082
-That one.
-Okay, okay, we'll change it.

911
00:58:59,083 --> 00:59:01,124
Wait. Do you know the Garcias?

912
00:59:01,125 --> 00:59:02,916
Yeah. That's the company we're buying.

913
00:59:04,833 --> 00:59:06,874
I thought you had all the land you needed.

914
00:59:06,875 --> 00:59:08,832
Yeah, the Garcias own
some of the most valuable docks

915
00:59:08,833 --> 00:59:10,874
-on the island.
-And we can't build the hotel

916
00:59:10,875 --> 00:59:12,458
unless we buy them.

917
00:59:17,166 --> 00:59:19,082
That's the boy you're seeing?

918
00:59:19,083 --> 00:59:20,916
A Garcia?

919
00:59:24,250 --> 00:59:27,040
-Lena, can I get the room?
-Of course.

920
00:59:27,041 --> 00:59:29,874
Excuse me. Would you just mind
following me and showing me...

921
00:59:29,875 --> 00:59:31,790
-Honey, I...
-No, Mom, please don't do this.

922
00:59:31,791 --> 00:59:33,332
I know the situation. Don't...

923
00:59:33,333 --> 00:59:34,790
Honey, this is for the best, okay?

924
00:59:34,791 --> 00:59:36,374
Their business is...

925
00:59:36,375 --> 00:59:37,665
-it's over.
-No, it's not.

926
00:59:37,666 --> 00:59:39,540
They're just waiting for a loan.
They need more time.

927
00:59:39,541 --> 00:59:42,124
Another loan?

928
00:59:42,125 --> 00:59:44,416
That is just gonna put them
further into debt.

929
00:59:46,583 --> 00:59:48,624
I'm giving them independence. Okay?

930
00:59:48,625 --> 00:59:51,249
Freedom from being trapped
inside a failing business.

931
00:59:51,250 --> 00:59:52,832
But they're not trapped though.

932
00:59:52,833 --> 00:59:55,541
They love it here. They love what they do.

933
00:59:56,666 --> 01:00:00,374
To them, it's just...
it's not about money.

934
01:00:00,375 --> 01:00:02,165
It's so much more than that.

935
01:00:02,166 --> 01:00:03,957
It's family, and it's where they're from.

936
01:00:03,958 --> 01:00:07,374
No, I know. I know the Garcias.

937
01:00:07,375 --> 01:00:09,957
And I feel for them.

938
01:00:09,958 --> 01:00:11,832
Okay? I do.

939
01:00:11,833 --> 01:00:13,040
But between you and I,

940
01:00:13,041 --> 01:00:15,582
I offered them double
than what it's worth.

941
01:00:15,583 --> 01:00:16,749
I'm not the villain here.

942
01:00:16,750 --> 01:00:19,457
Mateo Garcia is never gonna have to work
another day in his life, nor his son.

943
01:00:19,458 --> 01:00:20,915
It's not about that.

944
01:00:20,916 --> 01:00:22,874
This is what makes them happy.

945
01:00:22,875 --> 01:00:25,375
Mom, this gives them purpose.

946
01:00:28,375 --> 01:00:31,749
You know,
it's easy to be idealistic, okay?

947
01:00:31,750 --> 01:00:34,166
But business is business.
It's-it's not personal.

948
01:00:36,166 --> 01:00:38,000
Please.

949
01:00:39,958 --> 01:00:41,416
Please.

950
01:00:43,208 --> 01:00:44,916
For me.

951
01:00:46,833 --> 01:00:50,250
Okay, look, I'll see what I can do,
but I'm not promising anything, okay?

952
01:00:54,125 --> 01:00:59,165
<i>♪ I'll catch the train again ♪</i>

953
01:00:59,166 --> 01:01:03,790
<i>♪ Starry-eyed
and I'm stalking your mind...</i>

954
01:01:03,791 --> 01:01:05,583
Can I talk to you about something?

955
01:01:07,875 --> 01:01:12,540
<i>♪ The light that you lead home ♪</i>

956
01:01:12,541 --> 01:01:13,707
<i>♪ Drink a jug...</i>

957
01:01:13,708 --> 01:01:18,499
Can we just have one day
where we forget it all?

958
01:01:18,500 --> 01:01:19,625
Please?

959
01:01:21,625 --> 01:01:22,874
Yeah.

960
01:01:59,375 --> 01:02:01,457
Ry, sweetie?

961
01:02:01,458 --> 01:02:03,165
Are you here? Hey.

962
01:02:03,166 --> 01:02:07,499
I have meetings all day,
but I wanted to see you before I left.

963
01:02:07,500 --> 01:02:09,499
Did you refill your meds? Oh.

964
01:02:09,500 --> 01:02:12,915
I got you two dresses,
this green and pink,

965
01:02:12,916 --> 01:02:15,374
so let me know which one
you want to wear to the fundraiser.

966
01:02:15,375 --> 01:02:18,207
Did you figure something out
for the Garcias?

967
01:02:18,208 --> 01:02:21,624
Not yet, but I am working on it, okay?

968
01:02:22,875 --> 01:02:24,457
Sorry, we're running late.

969
01:02:24,458 --> 01:02:25,499
Yeah, here.

970
01:02:25,500 --> 01:02:28,100
I'm gonna be busy today,
but why don't we have breakfast tomorrow.

971
01:02:29,416 --> 01:02:31,540
You feeling okay?

972
01:02:31,541 --> 01:02:33,665
You look a little pale.

973
01:02:33,666 --> 01:02:35,125
I'm good.

974
01:02:36,166 --> 01:02:38,290
Okay. I love you.

975
01:02:38,291 --> 01:02:40,124
See you later.

976
01:02:54,666 --> 01:02:56,208
<i>Do you trust me?</i>

977
01:02:57,291 --> 01:02:58,541
Yeah.

978
01:03:00,541 --> 01:03:02,416
Turn off the light.

979
01:03:05,208 --> 01:03:06,250
Okay.

980
01:03:15,958 --> 01:03:19,833
This... is my favorite feeling.

981
01:03:21,125 --> 01:03:24,250
You just melt into everything around you.

982
01:03:25,291 --> 01:03:28,375
It helps me forget about the problems
when the lights are on.

983
01:03:31,791 --> 01:03:34,791
It's good to face your fears, Oriah.

984
01:03:37,333 --> 01:03:39,915
How else can you overcome them?

985
01:04:00,166 --> 01:04:02,708
This is where we met.

986
01:04:05,083 --> 01:04:06,374
Wait here.

987
01:04:21,000 --> 01:04:23,249
If you can't swim, I can help you.

988
01:04:54,666 --> 01:04:56,124
Hey.

989
01:04:56,125 --> 01:04:58,207
<i>Why do you look
like you just got laid?</i>

990
01:04:58,208 --> 01:05:00,624
<i>Okay, spill the tea.</i>

991
01:05:00,625 --> 01:05:03,040
Let's just say we have
a lot of catching up to do.

992
01:05:03,041 --> 01:05:04,915
<i>What is happening on that island?</i>

993
01:05:04,916 --> 01:05:06,832
<i>Tell me everything.</i>

994
01:05:06,833 --> 01:05:08,708
Dude, I think I'm in love.

995
01:05:09,833 --> 01:05:12,707
Like, on a cellular level.

996
01:05:12,708 --> 01:05:16,124
<i>On a cell... Who even are you right now?</i>

997
01:05:16,125 --> 01:05:17,832
<i>Okay, what-what are you gonna do?</i>

998
01:05:17,833 --> 01:05:20,416
<i>Aren't you coming home
in a couple of days?</i>

999
01:05:21,500 --> 01:05:22,624
I don't know.

1000
01:05:22,625 --> 01:05:24,040
<i>Wow.</i>

1001
01:05:24,041 --> 01:05:25,874
<i>So this is serious?</i>

1002
01:05:25,875 --> 01:05:27,832
Romeo and Juliet serious.

1003
01:05:27,833 --> 01:05:29,624
<i>Wait, didn't one of them die?</i>

1004
01:05:29,625 --> 01:05:31,457
Hey, it's Lena.

1005
01:05:31,458 --> 01:05:33,790
-I have to go.
<i>-Okay, talk soon. Call me.</i>

1006
01:05:33,791 --> 01:05:35,000
Yeah?

1007
01:05:36,375 --> 01:05:38,624
Hi, Ry. Your mom's
not gonna make it this morning.

1008
01:05:38,625 --> 01:05:40,165
With the event tonight,

1009
01:05:40,166 --> 01:05:42,665
she's being pulled
in a million directions.

1010
01:05:42,666 --> 01:05:44,958
Look, I know it's not my place to say...

1011
01:05:46,000 --> 01:05:47,582
but...

1012
01:05:47,583 --> 01:05:49,916
the Garcias have agreed to sell.

1013
01:05:51,500 --> 01:05:53,708
They're signing with Redwyn now.

1014
01:05:54,833 --> 01:05:56,707
-What?
-I'm so sorry, Ry.

1015
01:05:56,708 --> 01:05:57,790
I have to go.

1016
01:06:18,833 --> 01:06:20,790
No.

1017
01:06:32,375 --> 01:06:33,625
Julian!

1018
01:06:34,708 --> 01:06:36,791
Julian, what happened?

1019
01:06:37,875 --> 01:06:39,790
Who did this?

1020
01:06:39,791 --> 01:06:41,999
It was Carlos.

1021
01:06:42,000 --> 01:06:43,416
Last night.

1022
01:06:45,041 --> 01:06:46,250
Now my father...

1023
01:06:48,625 --> 01:06:50,458
It was the final straw.

1024
01:06:51,458 --> 01:06:53,541
He signed with Redwyn.

1025
01:07:00,375 --> 01:07:01,541
It's all my fault.

1026
01:07:05,000 --> 01:07:06,291
No.

1027
01:07:08,333 --> 01:07:09,500
No, it's not.

1028
01:07:14,625 --> 01:07:16,291
Julian, my mom works for Redwyn.

1029
01:07:22,833 --> 01:07:24,374
I'm so sorry. I just found out...

1030
01:07:24,375 --> 01:07:26,040
You need to leave, Ry.

1031
01:07:26,041 --> 01:07:28,540
-What? But I just...
-Leave!

1032
01:07:28,541 --> 01:07:29,708
Leave.

1033
01:07:39,583 --> 01:07:41,290
Mom?

1034
01:07:41,291 --> 01:07:42,707
Mom, what happened?

1035
01:07:42,708 --> 01:07:45,540
Could you give me a moment? Thank you.

1036
01:07:45,541 --> 01:07:47,457
You promised you would help them.

1037
01:07:47,458 --> 01:07:48,874
Honey, I did.

1038
01:07:48,875 --> 01:07:51,249
They had a sinking business,
and I threw them a lifeline.

1039
01:07:51,250 --> 01:07:53,540
Oh, so now
they have money and things

1040
01:07:53,541 --> 01:07:55,332
and no pride and no roots, just like you.

1041
01:07:55,333 --> 01:07:56,624
What does that mean?

1042
01:07:56,625 --> 01:07:59,040
It means you measure everything
with money.

1043
01:07:59,041 --> 01:08:02,040
You love power.
You're this power suit boss.

1044
01:08:02,041 --> 01:08:04,249
You brought me
to where you're from,

1045
01:08:04,250 --> 01:08:06,458
and you've barely left the hotel.

1046
01:08:08,541 --> 01:08:10,333
Why do you even do all of this?

1047
01:08:11,916 --> 01:08:13,707
Why?

1048
01:08:13,708 --> 01:08:16,291
Why do I do this? I do this for you.

1049
01:08:18,041 --> 01:08:20,124
How do you not see that?

1050
01:08:20,125 --> 01:08:22,332
You think I like being busy all the time?

1051
01:08:22,333 --> 01:08:25,540
Of course I want to spend time with you.

1052
01:08:25,541 --> 01:08:28,457
But I also thank God every day
that I have this job,

1053
01:08:28,458 --> 01:08:30,624
which I'm really good at,

1054
01:08:30,625 --> 01:08:32,582
because that means
I can take care of you, Ry.

1055
01:08:32,583 --> 01:08:35,250
In every way that you need.

1056
01:08:38,708 --> 01:08:40,125
You're my purpose.

1057
01:08:41,208 --> 01:08:42,375
Okay? So...

1058
01:08:43,916 --> 01:08:46,040
If I could've changed
the outcome for the Garcias,

1059
01:08:46,041 --> 01:08:47,375
I would have.

1060
01:08:48,875 --> 01:08:50,333
Believe me, I would have.

1061
01:08:55,583 --> 01:08:58,166
So let's... let's just
take a deep breath...

1062
01:08:59,916 --> 01:09:02,540
and get ready for the gala.

1063
01:09:02,541 --> 01:09:05,249
It is such an important night.

1064
01:09:05,250 --> 01:09:08,500
We only have a few days left here,
and I need you.

1065
01:10:23,958 --> 01:10:25,208
Oh.

1066
01:10:26,416 --> 01:10:28,665
I know you were having,
like, a super intense

1067
01:10:28,666 --> 01:10:30,624
mirror stare-off thing with yourself,

1068
01:10:30,625 --> 01:10:34,875
but for the record, you look hot.

1069
01:10:36,333 --> 01:10:39,582
And none of this is your fault,
by the way.

1070
01:10:39,583 --> 01:10:42,707
This is just the way the world works.

1071
01:10:42,708 --> 01:10:45,415
If it wasn't you guys,
it would've just been somebody else.

1072
01:10:45,416 --> 01:10:47,249
Hmm?

1073
01:10:47,250 --> 01:10:48,666
Probably uglier.

1074
01:10:49,791 --> 01:10:52,790
Julian will come around.

1075
01:10:52,791 --> 01:10:54,749
I promise.

1076
01:11:35,291 --> 01:11:36,458
No.

1077
01:11:37,791 --> 01:11:39,165
Fucking chemicals.

1078
01:11:53,375 --> 01:11:55,624
What do you want?

1079
01:11:55,625 --> 01:11:57,582
You know...

1080
01:11:57,583 --> 01:11:59,582
your boyfriend...

1081
01:11:59,583 --> 01:12:00,958
he owes me a lot of money.

1082
01:12:02,166 --> 01:12:04,665
And since you seem so fond
of his beautiful face,

1083
01:12:04,666 --> 01:12:07,541
I thought you'd like to stop me
from ruining it, no?

1084
01:12:08,625 --> 01:12:09,832
You'll get your money.

1085
01:12:09,833 --> 01:12:12,665
Slow down, <i>reina.</i>

1086
01:12:12,666 --> 01:12:15,290
Not everything has to be about cash.

1087
01:12:15,291 --> 01:12:17,749
Some things are worth more than money.

1088
01:12:17,750 --> 01:12:19,957
Like food, wine, women.

1089
01:12:19,958 --> 01:12:21,333
Get off of me.

1090
01:12:24,375 --> 01:12:26,915
If you touch her again, I'll kill you.

1091
01:12:26,916 --> 01:12:28,166
You understand?

1092
01:12:31,750 --> 01:12:33,708
Your money.

1093
01:12:38,166 --> 01:12:39,624
Shame.

1094
01:12:39,625 --> 01:12:41,416
She would have been fun.

1095
01:12:44,666 --> 01:12:46,165
Now get the fuck out of here!

1096
01:12:46,166 --> 01:12:48,790
You've got no reason
to come near us again.

1097
01:12:48,791 --> 01:12:49,957
Sure.

1098
01:12:49,958 --> 01:12:51,999
Until next time.

1099
01:12:55,458 --> 01:12:57,624
-You okay? You okay?
-I'm okay.

1100
01:12:57,625 --> 01:12:59,582
-You sure?
-I'm okay. I'm okay.

1101
01:12:59,583 --> 01:13:01,000
I'm okay.

1102
01:13:04,000 --> 01:13:05,415
Nice slap, by the way.

1103
01:13:07,416 --> 01:13:10,124
Remind me to never make you mad.

1104
01:13:16,041 --> 01:13:18,875
I'm really sorry about
not telling you about my mom.

1105
01:13:19,875 --> 01:13:21,874
I really thought I could fix it.

1106
01:13:21,875 --> 01:13:23,415
It's okay.

1107
01:13:23,416 --> 01:13:25,083
It's not your fault.

1108
01:13:41,333 --> 01:13:42,375
Your dress.

1109
01:13:44,000 --> 01:13:45,208
It's ruined.

1110
01:13:46,791 --> 01:13:49,749
I was passing on
your ecological complaint.

1111
01:13:51,041 --> 01:13:53,415
That whole thing about the grass
and the chemicals.

1112
01:13:53,416 --> 01:13:54,625
Wow.

1113
01:14:03,541 --> 01:14:05,958
I need you now.

1114
01:15:11,958 --> 01:15:13,166
Cheers.

1115
01:15:23,791 --> 01:15:25,290
Yeah.

1116
01:15:25,291 --> 01:15:28,582
It never ceases to amaze
what rich people will leave behind.

1117
01:15:28,583 --> 01:15:30,499
That lost and found is a treasure trove.

1118
01:15:30,500 --> 01:15:32,707
How do I look?

1119
01:15:37,791 --> 01:15:39,790
I'll see you guys down there.

1120
01:15:55,916 --> 01:15:57,499
I'm just wondering if there's a way.

1121
01:15:57,500 --> 01:15:59,665
I agree, but I'm worried
that it's too late.

1122
01:15:59,666 --> 01:16:02,082
You ready?

1123
01:16:02,083 --> 01:16:03,500
Let's do it.

1124
01:16:04,500 --> 01:16:06,165
Mom?

1125
01:16:06,166 --> 01:16:09,957
I want to introduce you to Julian Garcia.

1126
01:16:09,958 --> 01:16:12,707
It's a pleasure to meet you, <i>Señora Pera.</i>

1127
01:16:12,708 --> 01:16:14,458
I've heard a lot about you.

1128
01:16:16,375 --> 01:16:18,375
Let me get you both a drink.

1129
01:16:24,750 --> 01:16:28,332
Did you tell him who I am
and my association with Redwyn?

1130
01:16:28,333 --> 01:16:30,125
Yeah.

1131
01:16:31,583 --> 01:16:34,333
Did you tell him about your epilepsy?

1132
01:16:42,041 --> 01:16:43,832
<i>Gracias.</i>

1133
01:16:46,416 --> 01:16:48,707
<i>Buenas noches.</i> Good evening.

1134
01:16:48,708 --> 01:16:52,207
Thank you all for-for being here with us
to celebrate

1135
01:16:52,208 --> 01:16:55,582
this exciting new chapter for Mallorca.

1136
01:16:55,583 --> 01:16:59,582
We are thrilled to introduce
an arts center that will

1137
01:16:59,583 --> 01:17:03,290
preserve the cultural heartbeat
of this beautiful island.

1138
01:17:03,291 --> 01:17:07,165
Now, some of you know I grew up here,
a long time ago,

1139
01:17:07,166 --> 01:17:10,874
so it's nice to have a chance
to be able to give back,

1140
01:17:10,875 --> 01:17:14,915
and not only with this amazing arts center

1141
01:17:14,916 --> 01:17:18,957
but by bringing
a world-class resort to Mallorca.

1142
01:17:18,958 --> 01:17:22,832
So let's raise a glass

1143
01:17:22,833 --> 01:17:24,375
and make a...

1144
01:17:27,666 --> 01:17:30,249
and let's make a toast.

1145
01:17:30,250 --> 01:17:31,957
To Mallorca.

1146
01:17:31,958 --> 01:17:34,499
To Mallorca.

1147
01:17:48,583 --> 01:17:49,790
Mateo.

1148
01:17:49,791 --> 01:17:51,125
<i>¿Cómo estás?</i>

1149
01:17:54,708 --> 01:17:56,708
It's really good to see you.

1150
01:17:58,583 --> 01:18:00,958
I never thought I would see you again.

1151
01:18:02,333 --> 01:18:03,750
It's been a long time.

1152
01:18:04,750 --> 01:18:06,166
Yes.

1153
01:18:08,791 --> 01:18:11,832
Um, look, I want to...

1154
01:18:11,833 --> 01:18:13,790
let you know that
none of this was personal.

1155
01:18:13,791 --> 01:18:16,040
Isolde...

1156
01:18:16,041 --> 01:18:18,791
everything between us is personal.

1157
01:18:21,666 --> 01:18:24,874
I mean, I just want
to explain my intentions.

1158
01:18:24,875 --> 01:18:25,999
You don't need to explain anything.

1159
01:18:26,000 --> 01:18:28,332
I mean, you're right.

1160
01:18:28,333 --> 01:18:31,832
The island is changing,
and I can't keep it up anyways.

1161
01:18:31,833 --> 01:18:33,250
I tried.

1162
01:18:34,250 --> 01:18:36,958
I held on to my business
as long as I could.

1163
01:18:38,125 --> 01:18:39,916
But in the end...

1164
01:18:43,916 --> 01:18:46,749
-I just have one thing to ask of you.
-Yeah?

1165
01:18:46,750 --> 01:18:50,957
When you're building the hotel,
when you're shaping what comes next,

1166
01:18:50,958 --> 01:18:52,958
just don't forget about
what was here before.

1167
01:18:54,958 --> 01:18:57,375
I could never forget what was here before.

1168
01:18:58,666 --> 01:19:01,708
There is one good thing to come of this.

1169
01:19:03,041 --> 01:19:07,083
Maybe they will have the future
we never could.

1170
01:19:15,416 --> 01:19:17,124
Let's go.

1171
01:19:17,125 --> 01:19:19,540
This suit makes me feel like
I'm in a straitjacket.

1172
01:19:22,750 --> 01:19:24,374
Go be with your dad.

1173
01:19:24,375 --> 01:19:26,375
I'll find you later at the docks.

1174
01:19:27,833 --> 01:19:29,500
-See you later.
-Bye.

1175
01:19:37,791 --> 01:19:42,166
I thought you said your stories about
growing up here would bore me.

1176
01:19:51,958 --> 01:19:53,790
Mateo Garcia.

1177
01:19:55,000 --> 01:19:57,207
He was my first love.

1178
01:19:57,208 --> 01:20:01,874
We met when we were kids,
and as teenagers we couldn't...

1179
01:20:01,875 --> 01:20:03,875
stay away from each other.

1180
01:20:05,916 --> 01:20:10,374
He was the air I breathed
and the water I swam in.

1181
01:20:12,208 --> 01:20:15,666
We always talked about the future,
and we made plans and...

1182
01:20:19,000 --> 01:20:21,416
And then everything changed.

1183
01:20:22,458 --> 01:20:23,916
Your mom died.

1184
01:20:25,833 --> 01:20:29,333
I had never experienced a pain like that.

1185
01:20:32,166 --> 01:20:35,333
And every part of the island
just reminded me of her.

1186
01:20:38,583 --> 01:20:40,249
I had to leave. I had to escape.

1187
01:20:40,250 --> 01:20:42,957
Just wanted to get away.

1188
01:20:42,958 --> 01:20:44,540
I asked him to come with me.

1189
01:20:44,541 --> 01:20:46,332
I begged him.

1190
01:20:48,833 --> 01:20:52,250
He didn't want to leave his family
or the business.

1191
01:20:54,625 --> 01:20:58,290
We wrote letters for years,
back and forth,

1192
01:20:58,291 --> 01:21:00,083
and then one day the letters stopped.

1193
01:21:06,791 --> 01:21:09,874
So when I found out
we were building this hotel

1194
01:21:09,875 --> 01:21:13,333
and buying the land,
I jumped at the chance to help him.

1195
01:21:15,666 --> 01:21:18,415
I wish you would have told me.

1196
01:21:18,416 --> 01:21:19,832
Yeah.

1197
01:21:19,833 --> 01:21:24,082
And now I'm just the face
that stole his family's dreams.

1198
01:21:24,083 --> 01:21:25,875
No. No.

1199
01:21:31,000 --> 01:21:34,082
You did your best, Mom.

1200
01:21:34,083 --> 01:21:35,832
And he knows it.

1201
01:21:35,833 --> 01:21:37,082
Yeah.

1202
01:21:42,291 --> 01:21:44,915
<i>♪ All summer ♪</i>

1203
01:21:44,916 --> 01:21:47,250
<i>♪ your love burned alone...</i>

1204
01:21:49,000 --> 01:21:51,457
Can we stay up tonight?

1205
01:21:51,458 --> 01:21:52,625
Mm-hmm.

1206
01:21:53,875 --> 01:21:55,500
I've never seen a sunrise.

1207
01:21:56,916 --> 01:21:59,207
What do you mean?

1208
01:21:59,208 --> 01:22:00,333
From the water?

1209
01:22:01,583 --> 01:22:02,875
From anywhere.

1210
01:22:05,375 --> 01:22:06,791
Well...

1211
01:22:08,375 --> 01:22:11,124
I can get you
the best seat in the house.

1212
01:22:11,125 --> 01:22:13,915
-Hmm?
-Mm-hmm.

1213
01:22:13,916 --> 01:22:17,375
<i>♪ Beside the girl ♪</i>

1214
01:22:19,708 --> 01:22:22,665
<i>♪ Did you wait for ♪</i>

1215
01:22:22,666 --> 01:22:25,416
<i>♪ something to change you? ♪</i>

1216
01:22:28,500 --> 01:22:31,790
<i>♪ All the while you wait ♪</i>

1217
01:22:31,791 --> 01:22:33,583
<i>♪ for your heart ♪</i>

1218
01:22:36,833 --> 01:22:40,082
<i>♪ All the while you wait ♪</i>

1219
01:22:40,083 --> 01:22:43,374
<i>♪ for your heart to... ♪</i>

1220
01:22:43,375 --> 01:22:44,582
Look.

1221
01:22:44,583 --> 01:22:46,208
<i>♪ Wake up...</i>

1222
01:22:48,666 --> 01:22:51,415
<i>♪ For your heart ♪</i>

1223
01:22:51,416 --> 01:22:54,541
<i>♪ to wake up ♪</i>

1224
01:22:56,000 --> 01:22:59,375
Thank you for saving
your first sunrise for me.

1225
01:23:01,666 --> 01:23:04,790
You can have all my firsts
and all my lasts.

1226
01:23:38,041 --> 01:23:39,750
Mom, is everything okay?

1227
01:23:40,916 --> 01:23:43,166
When did you stop taking your meds?

1228
01:23:50,583 --> 01:23:53,041
A few days after we arrived.

1229
01:23:56,666 --> 01:23:58,374
They made me feel numb.

1230
01:23:58,375 --> 01:24:00,832
Mom, I needed a single summer
of feeling something.

1231
01:24:00,833 --> 01:24:01,915
I'm such an idiot.

1232
01:24:01,916 --> 01:24:03,374
I should have never left you alone.

1233
01:24:03,375 --> 01:24:05,082
-Stop. No.
-I should've stayed on top of you...

1234
01:24:05,083 --> 01:24:06,749
-It's my decision!
-to make sure you took your pills!

1235
01:24:06,750 --> 01:24:08,540
No. It's my decision.

1236
01:24:08,541 --> 01:24:10,707
You probably made everything worse!

1237
01:24:10,708 --> 01:24:13,499
I don't care.
I don't care.

1238
01:24:13,500 --> 01:24:14,749
-I care.
-I don't.

1239
01:24:14,750 --> 01:24:16,165
Okay.

1240
01:24:16,166 --> 01:24:18,415
-What are you doing?
-Let's go. We're leaving.

1241
01:24:18,416 --> 01:24:19,665
No, no, we're not.

1242
01:24:19,666 --> 01:24:22,082
-We're leaving.
-No. No, please.

1243
01:24:22,083 --> 01:24:23,832
Mom, I saw the sun rise
for the first time.

1244
01:24:23,833 --> 01:24:25,457
You did? That's great.

1245
01:24:25,458 --> 01:24:27,249
I can feel things.
I can feel Julian touching me,

1246
01:24:27,250 --> 01:24:30,374
and I could feel the sea on my skin.

1247
01:24:30,375 --> 01:24:33,666
At least there's something
worth remembering.

1248
01:24:35,750 --> 01:24:38,250
I want to stay here.

1249
01:24:40,291 --> 01:24:42,458
I want to live.

1250
01:24:43,500 --> 01:24:45,749
You want to stay here?

1251
01:24:45,750 --> 01:24:48,124
Oh, you want to live.
Now you want to live.

1252
01:24:48,125 --> 01:24:51,041
For how long, Ry?
How long do you want to live?

1253
01:24:52,083 --> 01:24:53,582
We're leaving.

1254
01:24:53,583 --> 01:24:55,250
I told Lena to move up our flight.

1255
01:24:56,583 --> 01:24:57,790
No.

1256
01:24:57,791 --> 01:24:59,207
Pack your stuff, Ry. Let's go.

1257
01:24:59,208 --> 01:25:01,124
No, Mom.

1258
01:25:01,125 --> 01:25:02,332
No.

1259
01:25:02,333 --> 01:25:03,666
Ry!

1260
01:25:07,458 --> 01:25:08,999
Ry!

1261
01:25:09,000 --> 01:25:10,207
Ry?

1262
01:25:11,625 --> 01:25:13,625
Ry, where are you going?

1263
01:25:16,416 --> 01:25:18,999
Ry? Ry!

1264
01:25:32,666 --> 01:25:34,500
Ry!

1265
01:26:02,000 --> 01:26:03,957
<i>Move, move, move! Ry!</i>

1266
01:26:05,125 --> 01:26:06,290
Hey, hey, hey. Shh.

1267
01:26:06,291 --> 01:26:08,790
It's okay. You're okay, baby. You're okay.

1268
01:26:08,791 --> 01:26:11,082
I'm right here. I'm right here.

1269
01:26:11,083 --> 01:26:13,040
Everything's gonna be okay.

1270
01:26:14,833 --> 01:26:16,040
I'm here.

1271
01:26:16,041 --> 01:26:17,833
There you are.

1272
01:26:20,916 --> 01:26:23,374
-Hi.
-Hey. Perfect timing.

1273
01:26:23,375 --> 01:26:24,999
I'm gonna go get a coffee.

1274
01:26:25,000 --> 01:26:26,499
Okay.

1275
01:26:26,500 --> 01:26:28,208
I'll be right back.

1276
01:26:31,541 --> 01:26:34,249
Oh. There she is.

1277
01:26:34,250 --> 01:26:37,165
Girl, I was high-key worried.

1278
01:26:37,166 --> 01:26:39,207
I would've come earlier,
but my boss made me

1279
01:26:39,208 --> 01:26:40,916
do, like, actual work.

1280
01:26:41,958 --> 01:26:44,749
You kept all this on the DL.

1281
01:26:44,750 --> 01:26:46,040
Ah?

1282
01:26:46,041 --> 01:26:48,665
Epilepsy and tubers?

1283
01:26:48,666 --> 01:26:50,874
Not to be confused with tumors,

1284
01:26:50,875 --> 01:26:53,166
although they sound just as shit.

1285
01:26:55,208 --> 01:26:56,999
I'm sorry for the secrets.

1286
01:26:57,000 --> 01:26:59,124
I get it.

1287
01:26:59,125 --> 01:27:01,040
You were looking for fun.

1288
01:27:01,041 --> 01:27:03,541
Which is why you gravitated to me. Hmm?

1289
01:27:06,541 --> 01:27:08,332
Speaking of fun, where's Prisha?

1290
01:27:08,333 --> 01:27:09,457
Is she here?

1291
01:27:09,458 --> 01:27:11,290
No.

1292
01:27:11,291 --> 01:27:14,374
All good things must come to an end.

1293
01:27:14,375 --> 01:27:15,540
She went home?

1294
01:27:15,541 --> 01:27:17,750
Yeah. But would I do it again?

1295
01:27:21,000 --> 01:27:22,250
Hell yeah, baby.

1296
01:28:04,083 --> 01:28:05,666
What happened?

1297
01:28:14,583 --> 01:28:15,791
Are you hurt?

1298
01:28:17,958 --> 01:28:20,125
I have tuberous sclerosis.

1299
01:28:22,041 --> 01:28:23,375
Causes epilepsy.

1300
01:28:24,666 --> 01:28:26,333
I was born with it.

1301
01:28:32,125 --> 01:28:34,415
What-what can we do?
Is there, is there a treatment?

1302
01:28:34,416 --> 01:28:36,957
Yes and no.

1303
01:28:36,958 --> 01:28:39,333
Medication helps,
but it's never been consistent.

1304
01:28:40,916 --> 01:28:43,499
And when I got here,
I stopped taking it altogether.

1305
01:28:43,500 --> 01:28:44,833
Why?

1306
01:28:46,416 --> 01:28:48,583
Because it made me
feel numb.

1307
01:28:50,083 --> 01:28:52,833
Julian, I don't want to feel numb anymore.

1308
01:28:59,958 --> 01:29:01,707
Is surgery an option?

1309
01:29:01,708 --> 01:29:05,165
Yes, but there's too much risk.

1310
01:29:05,166 --> 01:29:06,875
I could lose my memory.

1311
01:29:14,250 --> 01:29:16,082
So...

1312
01:29:16,083 --> 01:29:18,582
so would that be the worst thing?

1313
01:29:18,583 --> 01:29:19,750
You would be healthy.

1314
01:29:21,166 --> 01:29:23,500
Everything I know would be gone.

1315
01:29:29,916 --> 01:29:32,125
Why didn't you tell me any of this?

1316
01:29:35,416 --> 01:29:38,291
Because I wanted to figure it out...

1317
01:29:39,458 --> 01:29:41,500
for myself...

1318
01:29:43,041 --> 01:29:44,583
what I'm living for.

1319
01:29:47,083 --> 01:29:49,000
And it's this place.

1320
01:29:52,208 --> 01:29:53,625
It's...

1321
01:29:55,291 --> 01:29:58,708
It's watching my mom do what she loves.

1322
01:29:59,750 --> 01:30:03,250
It's watching Amara
try a new makeup trend.

1323
01:30:05,708 --> 01:30:08,625
It's sitting in a dark cave with you...

1324
01:30:10,000 --> 01:30:13,458
because you make darkness
feel peaceful.

1325
01:30:16,125 --> 01:30:18,083
Losing those memories...

1326
01:30:20,125 --> 01:30:22,708
or the ability to make new ones...

1327
01:30:27,125 --> 01:30:29,125
that's worse than death.

1328
01:30:42,541 --> 01:30:44,374
I love you, Oriah.

1329
01:30:50,458 --> 01:30:52,457
I love you, too.

1330
01:31:19,375 --> 01:31:20,458
Ry?

1331
01:31:35,541 --> 01:31:36,750
Ry.

1332
01:31:39,833 --> 01:31:41,625
Ry.

1333
01:31:44,916 --> 01:31:46,166
Ry.

1334
01:31:50,625 --> 01:31:51,833
Ry.

1335
01:31:53,291 --> 01:31:54,707
Ry!

1336
01:31:54,708 --> 01:31:56,290
No, no. Oriah!

1337
01:31:56,291 --> 01:31:57,500
Ry!

1338
01:32:01,708 --> 01:32:03,540
<i>Papá. Papá. Papá.</i>

1339
01:32:08,958 --> 01:32:10,165
Ry, please.

1340
01:32:16,166 --> 01:32:17,457
Faint pulse.

1341
01:32:17,458 --> 01:32:18,874
She stopped breathing at the scene

1342
01:32:18,875 --> 01:32:20,874
-but stabilized in transport.
-Stay with me, okay?

1343
01:32:20,875 --> 01:32:22,790
I'm gonna be here, okay?

1344
01:32:22,791 --> 01:32:24,915
<i>She's holding on, but barely.</i>

1345
01:32:24,916 --> 01:32:27,707
Scans show her condition has progressed.

1346
01:32:27,708 --> 01:32:31,125
It's your decision,
but we would strongly recommend surgery.

1347
01:32:34,375 --> 01:32:36,040
I mean, what is there to think about?

1348
01:32:36,041 --> 01:32:38,082
Ry has never wanted surgery.

1349
01:32:38,083 --> 01:32:41,790
I've tried to convince her for years,
and she made me promise.

1350
01:32:41,791 --> 01:32:45,707
We can stabilize her,
keep her comfortable.

1351
01:32:45,708 --> 01:32:48,415
But without surgery,
her condition will deteriorate,

1352
01:32:48,416 --> 01:32:51,082
and it will just be a matter of time.

1353
01:32:51,083 --> 01:32:53,083
Isolde...

1354
01:32:54,750 --> 01:32:57,249
I understand the risks,

1355
01:32:57,250 --> 01:33:00,083
and Oriah spoke to me about her wishes.

1356
01:33:01,333 --> 01:33:05,624
But while there is a chance
that we could save her

1357
01:33:05,625 --> 01:33:08,125
and a chance she could have
a normal life...

1358
01:33:10,041 --> 01:33:12,875
I beg you to take it.

1359
01:33:14,666 --> 01:33:18,791
She was worried about losing
the best parts of her life.

1360
01:33:19,833 --> 01:33:22,207
But if this works,

1361
01:33:22,208 --> 01:33:25,540
her favorite memories will be
the ones ahead of her.

1362
01:34:14,666 --> 01:34:17,500
She has the same condition
my mother had.

1363
01:34:18,541 --> 01:34:20,208
I'm so sorry, Izzy.

1364
01:34:24,875 --> 01:34:26,791
Does she know?

1365
01:34:28,250 --> 01:34:30,540
That I gave her this...

1366
01:34:30,541 --> 01:34:32,082
horrible thing that's hurting her?

1367
01:34:32,083 --> 01:34:33,500
No, she doesn't.

1368
01:34:34,750 --> 01:34:36,416
She wouldn't blame you.

1369
01:34:38,625 --> 01:34:41,041
You know, I never planned to have a baby.

1370
01:34:42,583 --> 01:34:43,832
Wasn't on my list.

1371
01:34:43,833 --> 01:34:46,249
No.

1372
01:34:46,250 --> 01:34:50,750
If I remember correctly, you wanted
a mansion, three cars and a pony.

1373
01:34:52,625 --> 01:34:53,833
I never got the pony.

1374
01:34:55,041 --> 01:34:58,165
When I found out I was pregnant, I...

1375
01:34:58,166 --> 01:35:00,333
I felt like my life had purpose.

1376
01:35:02,208 --> 01:35:04,208
And I wanted her so bad.

1377
01:35:05,750 --> 01:35:08,457
And I thought I would just
take the chance.

1378
01:35:08,458 --> 01:35:11,749
And you have raised a strong young woman

1379
01:35:11,750 --> 01:35:13,916
and gave her a wonderful life.

1380
01:35:16,291 --> 01:35:20,125
So whatever happens, Izzy,
you have nothing to be ashamed of.

1381
01:35:21,833 --> 01:35:23,583
Hmm? Nothing.

1382
01:36:02,125 --> 01:36:03,915
Hey, thanks for coming.

1383
01:36:03,916 --> 01:36:07,082
-No, of course.
-We have a lot of work to do.

1384
01:36:07,083 --> 01:36:08,957
Yeah, so we have a couple of solutions,

1385
01:36:08,958 --> 01:36:10,375
but they're pretty complex.

1386
01:36:14,708 --> 01:36:15,833
I'll take that one.

1387
01:36:29,208 --> 01:36:31,708
That is excellent news. Thank you.

1388
01:36:38,458 --> 01:36:40,540
-Julian.
-Isolde.

1389
01:36:40,541 --> 01:36:42,625
Hey. Sit down. Sit down.

1390
01:36:45,625 --> 01:36:47,041
I...

1391
01:36:49,791 --> 01:36:52,541
I have something that belongs to you.

1392
01:36:58,791 --> 01:37:00,999
When I was eight,

1393
01:37:01,000 --> 01:37:04,250
I found my father's letters
to his first love.

1394
01:37:05,625 --> 01:37:08,250
I always wondered who they were for.

1395
01:37:10,125 --> 01:37:13,250
And now I know who Izzy is.

1396
01:37:24,208 --> 01:37:25,291
Hey, guys.

1397
01:37:27,166 --> 01:37:28,374
Hey.

1398
01:37:28,375 --> 01:37:30,957
-You speak to the doctor?
-Uh, no.

1399
01:37:30,958 --> 01:37:33,499
No, I-I, um...

1400
01:37:33,500 --> 01:37:36,375
I haven't. There's been no-no change
with that, but...

1401
01:37:38,000 --> 01:37:41,416
there has been a... a new development.

1402
01:37:48,375 --> 01:37:52,041
So you found a new plot of land
to build the hotel?

1403
01:37:54,916 --> 01:37:57,290
I know how much your business
means to you.

1404
01:37:57,291 --> 01:37:59,957
And I thought it was too late, but it's...

1405
01:37:59,958 --> 01:38:01,708
it's never too late.

1406
01:38:04,125 --> 01:38:05,374
You were right.

1407
01:38:05,375 --> 01:38:07,166
This is my home.

1408
01:38:08,166 --> 01:38:10,290
And I should be protecting it.

1409
01:38:10,291 --> 01:38:12,332
So...

1410
01:38:12,333 --> 01:38:15,082
we are investing in your business.

1411
01:38:16,583 --> 01:38:18,583
It's what Ry would want.

1412
01:38:19,708 --> 01:38:21,666
It's what I want.

1413
01:38:23,208 --> 01:38:25,207
I think...

1414
01:38:25,208 --> 01:38:27,207
